EVEngine Dual License
=====================

Copyright (c) 2024-2026 西风逍遥游 <sunxfancy@gmail.com>
Copyright (c) 2024-2026 EVEngine Contributors

EVEngine (Evolutionary Vision Engine) is released under a **dual licensing** model.
You must choose one of the following according to your use:

1. **Free License** — see [LICENSE-OPENSOURCE](LICENSE-OPENSOURCE)
2. **Commercial License** — see [LICENSE-COMMERCIAL](LICENSE-COMMERCIAL)

Selection rules (summary)
-------------------------

| Your use | Applicable license | Cost |
|----------|--------------------|------|
| Open-source project use / integration; **or** a project using this Software with **annual revenue not exceeding RMB 100,000** | LICENSE-OPENSOURCE | **Free** |
| Project annual revenue **exceeding RMB 100,000**; or other cases requiring a commercial license | LICENSE-COMMERCIAL | **Paid; written authorization required** |
| Unsure | Contact the copyright holder | — |

Revenue threshold
-----------------

- “Annual Revenue” means the total operating revenue of the product / project that uses this Software in a calendar year (including sales, subscriptions, in-app purchases, advertising, licensing fees, crowdfunding proceeds, and all other revenue related to that product, without deducting costs).
- If Annual Revenue is **≤ RMB 100,000**, the Free License may continue to apply.
- Once Annual Revenue **exceeds** RMB 100,000, you must apply for and complete a Commercial License with the copyright holder within **one (1) month** from the date that threshold is exceeded; if you fail to do so in time, you **may not continue to use** this Software (including continued development, builds, runtime redistribution, and commercial distribution).

Notes
-----

- Third-party dependencies remain under their own licenses; this dual license covers only EVEngine’s original code and assets.
- Acceptance of either license means you have read and agree to all of its terms.

Commercial licensing contact
----------------------------

Email: sunxfancy@gmail.com  
Project: https://github.com/EVEngine/EVEngine
